errace seating, and use the elevated view to place the buildings you will revisit during the term.","short_summary":"A quiet outdoor reset doubles as a visual introduction to the campus layout.","evidence_claim":"Kettering documents a 1,600-square-foot rooftop terrace in the Learning Commons with seating, green space, hammocks, and electrical outlets.","source_url":"https://www.kettering.edu/who-we-are/campus-facilities/learning-commons","source_title":"Learning Commons","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Student ID access may be required on weekends; terrace availability can depend on building access and weather.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"kettering-connie-jim-john-recreation-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Connie and Jim John Recreation Center","title":"Saturday: Try One Recreation Option","subtitle":"Choose a low-pressure activity inside the student facility","notes":"Walk the suspended track or bring court gear, then note the equipment desk and locker-room locations for your next visit.","short_summary":"A short activity break introduces the recreation resources available to Kettering students.","evidence_claim":"The university says the private Recreation Center serves Kettering students, faculty, staff, and their families and includes courts, a walking track, fitness rooms, and a pool.","source_url":"https://www.kettering.edu/who-we-are/campus-facilities/recreation-center","source_title":"Recreation Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use is limited to eligible Kettering community members and authorized family members; consult the linked current-hours schedule before going.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"flint-farmers-market","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Flint Farmers’ Market","title":"Saturday: Explore the Public Market","subtitle":"Make a daytime trip to a year-round Flint destination","notes":"Go during market hours, browse the permanent vendors first, and agree on a meeting point before splitting up to compare food options.","short_summary":"The market offers an approachable daytime introduction to Flint’s vendors and public spaces.","evidence_claim":"The market’s official site describes it as a year-round public market at 300 East First Street with more than 50 vendors, open Tuesday, Thursday, and Saturday from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m.","source_url":"https://www.flintfarmersmarket.com/about-the-market/","source_title":"About The Market","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Current market hours are Tuesday, Thursday, and Saturday, 9 a.m.–5 p.m.; verify holiday changes on the official site.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"kettering-atwood-stadium","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Atwood Stadium at Kettering University","title":"Saturday: Find the Stadium Gate","subtitle":"Learn where campus recreation and Flint events meet","notes":"Walk the public-facing exterior, locate the entrance and posted rules, and return only for a scheduled event or authorized activity.","short_summary":"A daylight orientation stop makes future games and campus programs easier to navigate.","evidence_claim":"Kettering identifies Atwood Stadium as an 11,000-seat venue in Flint’s Carriage Town district used by university intramural and recreational programs and community teams.","source_url":"https://www.kettering.edu/who-we-are/campus-facilities/atwood-stadium","source_title":"Kettering University's Atwood Stadium","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":n